FIX-01: Keep one pipe's integration error from being lost to the next pipe's success

MSXchem_react() reacts the pipes in an OpenMP loop, and every pipe's
call wrote its return code into one shared errcode. An integration error
(513) or equilibrium error (514) in one pipe was overwritten by the next
pipe's 0, with one thread as with many, so the run carried on with
concentrations that were never solved. Each thread now keeps its own code,
and the largest code found is returned, whatever the number of threads.

A model that appears to run today can stop with error 513 or 514 once this
is applied. The error is real: it was there before, and was being lost.
Results are unchanged on every benchmark case, which have no such errors.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, on its own:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn FIX-01.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

diff --git a/src/solver/msxchem.c b/src/solver/msxchem.c
index 3fca3e3..44ce617 100644
--- a/src/solver/msxchem.c
+++ b/src/solver/msxchem.c
@@ -279,8 +279,12 @@ int MSXchem_react(double dt)
     }
 
 // --- examine each link
+//     (the largest error code found is returned whatever the number
+//     of threads, as the order in which links are done may vary)
+
 #pragma omp parallel
 {
+    int ierr;
     #pragma omp for private(k)
     for (k = 1; k <= MSX.Nobjects[LINK]; k++)
     {
@@ -293,10 +297,17 @@ int MSXchem_react(double dt)
         //evalHydVariables(k);
         for (int hi = 1; hi < MAX_HYD_VARS; hi++)
             HydVar[hi] = MSX.Link[k].HydVar[hi];
-         // --- compute pipe reactions
 
-         errcode = evalPipeReactions(k, dt);
-        //if (errcode) return errcode;
+        // --- compute pipe reactions
+
+        ierr = evalPipeReactions(k, dt);
+        if (ierr)
+        {
+            #pragma omp critical
+            {
+                if (ierr > errcode) errcode = ierr;
+            }
+        }
     }
 }
     if (errcode) return errcode;
